Project Documentation Phase – PocketSmart AI

The Project Documentation Phase involves preparing all the necessary documents related to PocketSmart AI: Your Smart Budget & Recommendation Assistant. The documentation explains the purpose, development process, features, testing, and final outcome of the project.

Documentation Activities

1. Project Introduction – Explain the concept and purpose of PocketSmart AI.


2. Problem Statement – Describe the problems users face in managing budgets and expenses.


3. Objectives – Document the goals and expected benefits of the system.


4. Requirement Analysis – Record the functional and non-functional requirements.


5. System Design – Include system architecture, database design, flowcharts, and diagrams.


6. Development Details – Explain the technologies, modules, and methods used to develop the system.


7. Testing Documentation – Record the testing methods, test cases, errors found, and corrections made.


8. Screenshots – Include screenshots of important pages such as login, dashboard, budget, expenses, and recommendations.


9. Results & Discussion – Explain the final performance and benefits of the system.


10. Conclusion & Future Scope – Summarize the project and mention possible future improvements.



Expected Outcome

The final documentation will provide a complete record of the PocketSmart AI project, making it easy to understand, evaluate, maintain, and present the project.
